**Plan, no changes made.**

`buildRows()` in [report.js](src/report.js) already carries the full data, `owner` and `slow` included. `toTable` in [format.js](src/format.js) drops those two on purpose, table's too narrow.

So `--json` should serialize `buildRows()` straight, not go through `toTable`. In [cli.js](src/cli.js):

```js
const json = argv.includes('--json');
const rows = buildRows();
process.stdout.write((json ? JSON.stringify(rows, null, 2) : toTable(rows)) + '\n');
```

That gives JSON the full row shape, table users see no change. Want me to apply it?
